WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:09.731
An embedding model maps text to a point on (or near) a high-dimensional sphere, trained contrastively so that related texts are close.

3
00:00:10.011 --> 00:00:20.635
On normalized vectors, dot product, cosine, and Euclidean distance are interchangeable for ranking; off the sphere they are not, so follow the model’s documentation.

4
00:00:20.915 --> 00:00:26.824
Scores are model-specific, so rank rather than threshold, and never mix models in one index.

5
00:00:27.104 --> 00:00:31.691
And a vector is a lossy summary: check it against real queries from your domain.

6
00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:37.752
Next lesson: how to pick among dozens of embedding models without trusting a leaderboard blindly.
